# Vulnerabilities govulncheck may report without failing the build.
#
# One OSV ID per line. Anything NOT listed here fails CI, so this file is the
# only way a finding is tolerated -- a new vulnerability cannot slip through.
#
# Review this list whenever vault/sdk is upgraded: both entries below exist
# only because the SDK drags the Docker client in, and they should be deleted
# the moment it stops doing so.

# GO-2026-4883  Moby: off-by-one in plugin privilege validation
# GO-2026-4887  Moby: AuthZ plugin bypass on oversized request bodies
#
# Both are flaws in the Docker DAEMON's plugin authorization. This plugin runs
# no daemon and makes no Docker API calls: `go mod why github.com/docker/docker`
# reports "main module does not need package", and every trace govulncheck
# prints is a package init() chain reached through
# hashicorp/vault/sdk -> helper/connutil, not a call into the vulnerable code.
#
# They cannot be fixed by upgrading. The fix is published as
# github.com/moby/moby/v2 v2.0.0-beta.8, a different module path, so
# github.com/docker/docker has no fixed version at all ("Fixed in: N/A").
# The requirement comes from hashicorp/vault/sdk v0.20.0 and
# hashicorp/go-secure-stdlib/plugincontainer v0.4.2, so it is not ours to drop
# and `go mod tidy` keeps it.
GO-2026-4883
GO-2026-4887
